+/**
+ * Moves a carousel between its items through their order and direction tokens, by call, key,
+ * swipe, or its own timer.
+ *
+ * @remarks
+ * The host must be an HTMLElement in the current realm and have no live carousel owner.
+ * Construction validates and copies the `classes`, `attributes`, and `selectors` groups, resolves
+ * the `interval`, `keyboard`, `pause`, `ride`, `touch`, and `wrap` options from the defaults, the
+ * attributes the `attributes` group names, and the constructor, claims the host, binds the hooks,
+ * and listens on the host: for the arrow keys when `keyboard` is true, for the pointer entering and
+ * leaving when `pause` is true, and, when `touch` is true, for swipes through a `Swipe` it
+ * constructs with its `pointer` token and for the drag of an item's image, and for a touch or pen
+ * release when `pause` is true as well. A swipe constructed while a reaction to its token write
+ * destroyed the carousel is destroyed at once. A `load` ride starts cycling. The items are the
+ * elements the `entry` selector matches inside the host that sit inside no other item, and the
+ * active item is the first of them carrying the `active` token, both read at each call. A slide
+ * dispatches the cancelable `slide.vn.carousel` event, moves the indicator, writes the incoming
+ * item's order token, the direction token to both items, waits for the incoming item's transition
+ * when the host carries the `slide` token, moves the `active` token, and dispatches
+ * `slid.vn.carousel`. A slide that another slide started inside its `slide.vn.carousel` dispatch
+ * took over resolves `false`. After each write and await, a slide reads its lifetime, that both
+ * items are still items of the host, and the tokens and indicator values the phase requires, and
+ * it stops, writing and dispatching nothing more, and resolves `false`, when any read fails. The
+ * timer is a chain of native timeouts at the active item's interval attribute or the `interval`
+ * option. Arming reads whether cycling is wanted, whether a touch deferral is pending, whether the
+ * pointer over the host holds it under `pause`, and whether the view prefers reduced motion, and
+ * arms nothing when any holds; each tick slides forward only while the document is visible and the
+ * host is rendered. Destruction restores the items and indicators before the swipe's token. An
+ * aborted `signal` destroys the carousel.
